q0001
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:10.980
When a benchmark says CM, is it timing a matrix, a program graph, or a wrapper that creates both?

q0002
00:00:10.980 --> 00:00:21.960
This episode has one job: The explicit CM is a dense truth-layout artifact; CM-IR is a canonicalized shared program graph that may later produce dense, flat, or packed outputs.

q0003
